:: TheCall {"title":"Chapter V / No Happy Endings","scene":"kitchen"}
@do $betrayed = true
@do $heat += 3
@do $trust -= 4
@do $notes.push({id: $notes.length, text: "Lenora gave Cal the interview address."})

# No happy endings

@Chapter("CHAPTER V · 8:17 A.M.", "The call")

Cal answers on the sixth ring.

You tell him Mars is using **his** truck to get a new job. You give him the address.
You tell yourself he deserves to know where his property is.

The interview ends in a parking lot with two police officers, one expired insurance
paper, and a truck registered to the absent Arthur. Nobody can prove ownership.
Everyone can prove Mars has the worst documents.

The truck leaves on the hook of another truck.

At dusk Mars returns without keys.

::: dialogue {.dialogue speaker="Mars" mood="quiet"}
“Cal repeated your sentence word for word. He has never built a sentence that clean.”
:::

[[Admit you wanted her trapped -> Rupture]]

[[Explain that the truck was never legally hers -> Justify]]

:: InterviewMorning {"title":"Chapter V / The Company Lot","scene":"yard"}
# The company lot

@Chapter("CHAPTER V · 8:53 A.M.", "A truck with clean paperwork")

The company lot contains twelve white trucks, each with matching doors and a reverse
alarm that works. Mars touches one fender as if it belongs to a gentler species.

The manager likes her. The record check does not. Jules's call keeps the conversation
alive, but only just.

The manager offers probationary shifts. Mars can start Tuesday, if she arrives without
the disputed truck and if somebody covers the uniform deposit.

@Pulse()

[[Pay the deposit. Do not call it rescue -> PayDeposit]]

[[Ask her to stay and make Sister Shift legitimate -> LegitimatePlan]]

@if ($heat >= 4) {
  [[Keep the apartment contracts; the money is finally real -> PredatoryPlan]]
}

:: PayDeposit {"title":"Finale / The Key on the Table","scene":"kitchen"}
@do $debt += 180
@do $honesty += 1
@do $trust += 1

@if ($honesty >= 4 && $trust >= 4) {
  [[Let her leave, then ask her to dinner somewhere neutral -> BetterThings]]
} @else {
  [[Let her leave without making the debt a leash -> KeyReturned]]
}

:: LegitimatePlan {"title":"Finale / Terms","scene":"kitchen"}
@do $debt += 900

@Chapter("FINAL OFFER", "A company of two")

You propose a new truck with clean papers, roadside assistance instead of ambush
towing, and a ledger that can survive daylight. Mars asks who owns what.

For once, you write it down before you answer.

@if ($honesty >= 3 && $heat <= 3) {
  [[Split it down the middle, including the exit clause -> TermsAndConditions]]
} @else {
  [[Put the house up as collateral -> BusinessPartners]]
}

:: PredatoryPlan {"title":"Finale / Sister Shift Recovery","scene":"yard"}
@do $debt -= 200
@do $heat += 3

@Chapter("FINAL OFFER", "The numbers finally work")

You show Mars the apartment contracts. She shows you the uniform deposit form.

One future pays less and might let her sleep. The other is already yours.

[[Choose the money you understand -> WomenOwned]]

[[Tear up the worst contract and take the Tuesday shift -> KeyReturned]]

:: Rupture {"title":"Finale / What It Was For","scene":"kitchen"}
@do $honesty += 2

@Chapter("AFTER THE CALL", "What it was for")

“I wanted you to come back,” you say. “I wanted the outside world to fail before you
could decide I was the failure.”

Mars packs the plastic basket. At the door she pauses.

@if ($honesty >= 3) {
  [[Give her the house key and do not ask where she is going -> HonestWreck]]
} @else {
  [[Tell her nobody else knows how to keep her safe -> LockedRoom]]
}

:: Justify {"title":"Finale / Legally Speaking","scene":"kitchen"}
@do $leverage += 2
@do $trust -= 2

@Chapter("AFTER THE CALL", "Legally speaking")

You explain the registration, the liability, and every risk you prevented. Mars
listens until your argument is flawless.

“You do not love me,” she says. “You love being the locked door and the spare key.”

[[Tell her to leave -> LockedRoom]]

[[Ask her to stay without using the word safe -> BusinessPartners]]

